   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 01. PySpark Fundamentals\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook introduces the core idea behind Spark: distributed data processing with lazy evaluation.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Learning goals\n",
    "- Understand Spark architecture\n",
    "- Learn how data flows in a Spark application\n",
    "- Distinguish transformations from actions\n",
    "- Use the SparkSession correctly\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Spark architecture\n",
    "\n",
    "Spark runs on a cluster of machines. The key components are:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Driver: the program that coordinates execution\n",
    "- Executors: worker processes that execute tasks\n",
    "- Cluster Manager: manages resources (YARN, Kubernetes, standalone, local)\n",
    "- Resilient Distributed Dataset (RDD): basic distributed unit of data\n",
    "- DataFrame: higher-level distributed table abstraction\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pyspark.sql import SparkSession\n",
    "\n",
    "spark = SparkSession.builder \\\n    " .appName('PySpark-Fundamentals') \\\n    " .master('local[*]') \\\n    " .config('spark.sql.shuffle.partitions', '4') \\\n    " .getOrCreate()\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Spark Version:', spark.version)\n",
    "spark.stop()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Lazy evaluation\n",
    "\n",
    "Spark does not execute transformations immediately. It builds a logical execution plan. Action triggers execution.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pyspark.sql import SparkSession\n",
    "\n",
    "spark = SparkSession.builder.appName('LazyEval').master('local[*]').getOrCreate()\n",
    "\n",
    "data = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\n",
    "rdd = spark.sparkContext.parallelize(data)\n",
    "\n",
    "mapped = rdd.map(lambda x: x * 2)\n",
    "filtered = mapped.filter(lambda x: x > 5)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('No execution yet; only plan built. Next action:')\n",
    "print(filtered.collect())\n",
    "\n",
    "spark.stop()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Transformations vs actions\n",
    "\n",
    "### Transformations\n",
    "- `map`\n",
    "- `filter`\n",
    "- `select`\n",
    "- `withColumn`\n",
    "- `groupBy`\n",
    "\n",
    "They create a new dataset without immediate execution.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Actions\n",
    "- `collect`\n",
    "- `count`\n",
    "- `show`\n",
    "- `take`\n",
    "- `save`\n",
    "\n",
    "They trigger execution and return results.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pyspark.sql import SparkSession\n",
    "\n",
    "spark = SparkSession.builder.appName('TransformActionDemo').master('local[*]').getOrCreate()\n",
    "\n",
    "df = spark.createDataFrame([(1, 'Alice'), (2, 'Bob')], ['id', 'name'])\n",
    "\n",
    "df2 = df.filter(df.id > 1)\n",
    "print('Filtered rows:')\n",
    "df2.show()\n",
    "print('Row count:', df2.count())\n",
    "\n",
    "spark.stop()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Why this matters\n",
    "\n",
    "Spark optimizes queries before execution. This means that a chain of transformations can be optimized as one plan, which is efficient for large datasets.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Exercise\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Create a DataFrame with 5 rows of sample customer data.\n",
    "2. Apply a filter on a field.\n",
    "3. Count the rows.\n",
    "4. Explain why the transformation is still lazy until `count()` or `show()`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pyspark.sql import SparkSession\n",
    "\n",
    "spark = SparkSession.builder.appName('Exercise').master('local[*]').getOrCreate()\n",
    "customers = [\n",
    "    (1, 'Alice', 2500),\n",
    "    (2, 'Bob', 3100),\n",
    "    (3, 'Charlie', 1800),\n",
    "    (4, 'Dana', 4200),\n",
    "    (5, 'Eve', 2600)\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "df = spark.createDataFrame(customers, ['customer_id', 'name', 'salary'])\n",
    "filtered = df.filter(df.salary > 2500)\n",
    "print(filtered.count())\n",
    "filtered.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "spark.stop()\n"
   ]
  }
 ],
